---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { loadElements } from '../lib/data'
import { href } from '../lib/site'

const elements = loadElements()
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Download — UN/TDED"
  description="The UNTDED 2005 dataset is available as YAML, CSV, JSON, JSON-LD and RDF Turtle, together with the source publication."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink">Download</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-body">
      The complete dataset is published in machine-readable formats, and every
      artifact below is generated from a single source.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-8 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <a
        href="https://github.com/untded/untded-2005"
        class="rounded-md border border-line bg-paper p-5 transition-colors hover:border-un/60"
      >
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">YAML: full dataset ↗</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
          The repository <span class="font-mono text-xs">untded/untded-2005</span>{' '}
          contains nine category files that cover every element, and each entry names
          its page in the source publication.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/untded/untded-2005/releases"
        class="rounded-md border border-line bg-paper p-5 transition-colors hover:border-un/60"
      >
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">CSV &amp; JSON exports ↗</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
          The release artifacts include{' '}
          <span class="font-mono text-xs">elements.csv</span>, with one row per element, and{' '}
          <span class="font-mono text-xs">elements.json</span>, with the full records;
          both are generated from the dataset.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href={href('/data/untded.jsonld')} class="rounded-md border border-line bg-paper p-5 transition-colors hover:border-un/60">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">JSON-LD</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
          The file <span class="font-mono text-xs">/data/untded.jsonld</span> carries the
          whole directory as a linked-data graph, in which every element is an
          identified resource that uses schema.org and UNTDED vocabulary terms.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href={href('/data/untded.ttl')} class="rounded-md border border-line bg-paper p-5 transition-colors hover:border-un/60">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">RDF Turtle</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
          The file <span class="font-mono text-xs">/data/untded.ttl</span> carries the
          same graph as Turtle for SPARQL stores and RDF tooling, and the YAML-LD
          context of the dataset defines the vocabulary.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href={href('/data/index.json')} class="rounded-md border border-line bg-paper p-5 transition-colors hover:border-un/60">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Compact index</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
          The file <span class="font-mono text-xs">/data/index.json</span> is a light
          JSON list of all {elements.length} elements, with the tag, name,
          representation, change tag, status and category of each.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href={href('/data/vocabulary.json')} class="rounded-md border border-line bg-paper p-5 transition-colors hover:border-un/60">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Vocabulary declaration</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
          The file <span class="font-mono text-xs">/data/vocabulary.json</span> publishes
          the ontology as data, with the prefixes, classes and properties generated
          from the single vocabulary declaration of the dataset.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href={href('/data/edifact-links.json')} class="rounded-md border border-line bg-paper p-5 transition-colors hover:border-un/60">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">UN/EDIFACT join</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
          The file <span class="font-mono text-xs">/data/edifact-links.json</span> carries
          the element-by-element join against the D.05B EDED mirror, with the
          representation-alignment verdict for every joined tag.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href={href('/data/uncl-coverage.json')} class="rounded-md border border-line bg-paper p-5 transition-colors hover:border-un/60">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">UNCL code coverage</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
          The file <span class="font-mono text-xs">/data/uncl-coverage.json</span> records
          which elements are code-qualified in the UN/EDIFACT D.05B code list and how
          many values each of them carries.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href={href('/data/uncl-refs.json')} class="rounded-md border border-line bg-paper p-5 transition-colors hover:border-un/60">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">UNCL cross-references</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
          The file <span class="font-mono text-xs">/data/uncl-refs.json</span> records the
          section 4.1.5 cross-references, which state which UNCL code values name a
          TDED element by the equals rule or by the related rule, from the full text of
          D.01B.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href={href('/ns/untded-context.jsonld')} class="rounded-md border border-line bg-paper p-5 transition-colors hover:border-un/60">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">JSON-LD context</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
          The file <span class="font-mono text-xs">/ns/untded-context.jsonld</span> is the
          context for citing TDED elements from JSON-LD, and it is pinned to this
          edition. The{' '}
          <a class="text-un-deep underline decoration-un/50" href={href('/guides/context')}>context guide</a>{' '}
          describes its use.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a href={href('/elements/1004/data.ttl')} class="rounded-md border border-line bg-paper p-5 transition-colors hover:border-un/60">
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Per-element RDF</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
          Every element resolves individually in both RDF syntaxes at{' '}
          <span class="font-mono text-xs">/elements/&lt;tag&gt;/data.ttl</span>{' '}
          and <span class="font-mono text-xs">data.jsonld</span>, and element{' '}
          <a class="text-un-deep underline decoration-un/50" href={href('/elements/1004')}>1004</a>{' '}
          is an example.
        </p>
      </a>
      <a
        href="https://github.com/untded/references"
        class="rounded-md border border-line bg-paper p-5 transition-colors hover:border-un/60"
      >
        <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Source publication ↗</h2>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
          The repository <span class="font-mono text-xs">untded/references</span>{' '}
          contains the PDF of the 2005 edition and the related reference documents.
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>

    <section class="mt-10 rounded-md border border-line bg-mist p-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-body">
      <h2 class="font-semibold text-ink">Attribution</h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        The content is UNTDED 2005, ECE/TRADE/362 (in parallel ISO 7372:2005),
        © United Nations / UNECE, and it is reproduced with attribution. The
        digitization is by this project, which is a member-contribution pilot to
        UN/CEFACT and ISO/TC 154 and is not an official publication. The code is
        released under the MIT license. A user of the dataset cites the source
        publication and this dataset.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
